  "verdict": "REPRODUCED at the matched budget: the in-house head-only K-curve is positive at every K (K=5 +0.0129 .. K=80 +0.0996) and family-significant at K=20,40,80; the same model at epochs=20 was negative at K=5/K=10, so the sign is set by the source budget, not the model.",
  "budget_note": "The chemprop reference this migrates trains its source model for config.epochs=50 (fsma_c4_head_k*.config.epochs).  The original in-house curve used epochs=20 and is NEGATIVE at K=5/K=10; at the matched epochs=50 budget the same model is positive at every K.  Both budgets are reported (inhouse_ep50 = primary, inhouse_ep20 = sensitivity) so the sign flip is visible rather than hidden.",
  "caveats": [
    "The adaptation step is NOT bit-reproducible on CUDA: two epochs=50 runs of the same config agree to ~1e-3 on the 50-cell mean but differ by up to 0.079 on an individual cell.  Only the aggregate is reported; per-cell values are noisy.",
    "Capacity is NOT matched to the chemprop reference (hidden=128 vs d_h=300) in the PRIMARY column; the hidden=512 capacity ablation is carried alongside.  For the ablation the criterion is the ADAPTED ABSOLUTE AUC (adapted_abs_auc per K), NOT the paired delta: a stronger source raises zero_shot_auc more than adapted_auc, so the delta shrinks at low K (K5 +0.0129 -> -0.0033) even though the absolute AUC rises.  The 'delta positive at every K' claim is made for the h128 primary only.",
    "The epochs=20 column is carried as a sensitivity, not discarded: it is the budget at which the in-house low-K delta is negative.",
    "chemprop v2 is a REFERENCE scorer here, not the paper's model (project red line: the method result is the in-house D-MPNN)."
  ],
